# p_phases_pinned_s5: diagnostic. s5 lever set with the allocator pinned (phases separated).
#
# basis      one plateau over two phases (per phase window):
#              p_census_peak_s5              conversion 2,062,680   inference 2,069,512
#              p_census_peak_s5_graphclear   conversion 2,056,000   inference 2,056,000
#            census at 97.9%: conversion = 431 MB float32 model + ~1.5 GB protobuf/serialisation
#            (crypten_modules=0); inference = 862 MB int64 weight shares + 318 MB activations
#            (crypten_modules=1493).
# hypothesis RSS high-water: conversion grows the process to 2.05 GB; inference reuses the arena.
# method     MALLOC_TRIM_THRESHOLD_=0 returns the arena between phases (each phase's own plateau). Not
#            a step (allocator knob refused 17.08.: [heap] -1,044 MB, anon +788 MB).
# outcomes   inference clearly lower -> import-bound; next target the protobuf parse
#            (plaintext_free_early showed the 433 MB model is not the holder). Level when pinned -> the
#            862 MB reloaded weight shares at inference are binding.
# run        PEAK_TRIGGER_PCT=0.
SHAFT_LEVERS=plaintext_free_cpu,triple_share_free_cpu,trace_nograd_cpu,onnx_single_file_export_cpu,encrypt_spill_cpu,embed_chunk_cpu,probe_census_cpu
SHAFT_INNER_ENV="SHAFT_EMBED_CHUNKS=16 MALLOC_ARENA_MAX=1 MALLOC_TRIM_THRESHOLD_=0 MALLOC_MMAP_THRESHOLD_=131072"
